@startuml

header "Private Group Message Flow (Phase 1+2: chat.groups Topic Exchange)"
footer "Author: Tuzaku | 2 users, 2 instances | Group 42"

actor "User1\n(Instance 1)" as User1
actor "User2\n(Instance 2)" as User2
participant "WebApp 1" as WebApp1
participant "WebApp 2" as WebApp2
participant "Instance 1" as App1
participant "Instance 2" as App2
participant "SimpleBroker 1" as Broker1
participant "SimpleBroker 2" as Broker2
participant "RabbitMQ\nBrokerHandler" as RabbitHandler
participant "RabbitMQ" as RabbitMQ
participant "Listener 1" as Listener1
participant "Listener 2" as Listener2
database PostgreSQL

note over User1, User2
  Both users are members of **group 42**.
  User1 is connected to Instance 1 (sender).
  User2 is connected to Instance 2 (receiver).
  RabbitMQ topology per instance:
  - exchange: chat.groups
  - queue: ws.{instance-id}.inbound
  - binding added when a user subscribes to /topic/group.42
end note

== 1. User2 subscribes to group chat ==

User2 -> WebApp2: Open group 42 chat
WebApp2 -> App2: STOMP SUBSCRIBE /topic/group.42
App2 -> App2: validateSubscription()\n(user is group member)
App2 -> RabbitHandler: handleSubscribe(..., "/topic/group.42")
RabbitHandler -> RabbitMQ: bind ws.instance-2.inbound\nto chat.groups, key "group.42"
App2 -> Broker2: Register local subscription
App2 -> WebApp2: SUBSCRIBE confirmed

== 2. User1 sends a group message ==

User1 -> WebApp1: Type and send message
WebApp1 -> App1: STOMP SEND /app/group.send\n{ groupId: 42, content: "..." }
App1 -> App1: validateGroup()\n(user is group member)
App1 -> PostgreSQL: saveGroupMessage()
PostgreSQL --> App1: saved

note over App1
  Delivery path (hybrid broker):
  1. SimpleBroker — local subscribers on Instance 1
  2. RabbitMQ — subscribers on other instances
end note

App1 -> Broker1: convertAndSend("/topic/group.42", response)
Broker1 -> WebApp1: MESSAGE (if User1 is subscribed locally)

App1 -> RabbitHandler: publishToRabbitMQ("/topic/group.42", response)
RabbitHandler -> RabbitMQ: publish chat.groups\nkey "group.42"\nheaders: source-instance-id, stomp-destination

== 3. Cross-instance delivery to User2 ==

RabbitMQ -> Listener1: ws.instance-1.inbound
Listener1 -> Listener1: source-instance-id = instance-1\n→ skip (same instance)

RabbitMQ -> Listener2: ws.instance-2.inbound
Listener2 -> Listener2: source-instance-id = instance-1\n→ forward
Listener2 -> Listener2: read stomp-destination\n→ /topic/group.42
Listener2 -> Broker2: convertAndSend("/topic/group.42", payload)
Broker2 -> WebApp2: MESSAGE
WebApp2 -> User2: Display message

@enduml
